 {"status":"in_progress","id":"AUG-178","title":"AUG-176's bulk registration left the `auger` DuckBrain namespace unsearchable (q= and contains= both exceed 120s; cos namespace answers a novel query in 11.4s)","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"c53293c02781481f7342459af25eb1dabdd2bba794c915b77945820476cb2452"},"priority":"P1","source":null,"reasoning":null,"review_notes":null,"ts":null,"acceptance_criteria":"WHY THIS ROW EXISTS: namespace `auger` answers ?q= and ?contains= with a hang (client rc=124 at 40-120s) while prefix reads stay fast, which blocks AUG-176 AC3. Root cause MEASURED 2026-11-17: a 0-byte pid-less `.search.rebuild.lock` in the LIVE namespace dir (/home/kara/duckbrain/namespaces/auger) is never stolen by src/search/index.ts:tryAcquireRebuildLock() because the steal condition requires `pid !== null`, so the sidecar rebuild waits forever; the sidecar was never built (.search held only fts.duckdb.tmp + rows.tmp.jsonl from 2026-10-30). The row's original ingest-chunking hypothesis is REFUTED. Evidence: evidence/AUG-178/{01,02,03}-*.txt.\n\nAC1 `timeout 120 curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}' -H \"x-api-key: <token>\" \"http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/memories?namespace=auger&q=<novel text>&limit=3\"` expects `200` with time_total < 5.0. PROOF: warm series 1.84/1.51/1.39/1.39/1.87s at loadavg 77 (cos control 1.52s). FAILIF: rc=124, or any warm run >= 5.0s.\nAC2 same call with `&contains=inbox` expects `200` with time_total < 5.0. PROOF: 0.402s total=31, and contains=rollback 0.497s total=100. FAILIF: rc=124 or >= 5.0s.\nAC3 ROOT CAUSE NAMED BY MEASUREMENT (corrected): evidence/AUG-178/02-root-cause-lock.txt names the pid-less lock and the missing sidecar as the cause and refutes the oversized-ingest hypothesis; the durable code fix is routed to the duckbrain repo via AUG-180 and is NOT applied by rewriting the substrate. PROOF: `ls -la /home/kara/duckbrain/namespaces/auger/.search` shows fts.duckdb + meta.json and no lock; `cat .../.search/meta.json` shows rowCount=2559, sourceFiles=24. FAILIF: any claim that the ingest rows caused the hang, or a substrate rewrite used as the fix.\nAC4 `python3 scripts/recall_battery.py` (AUG-176 worktree) runs to completion and writes per-project hit rates (target block in top-5) into evidence/AUG-176/06-recall-battery.md; every below-hit query carries a chunking/granularity fix or a named residual cause. PROOF: the committed report with a numeric hit rate per project. FAILIF: a missing report or asserted counts without the query list.\nAC5 NO FABRICATED EVIDENCE: probe transcripts are committed under evidence/AUG-178/, and registered/regenerable counts are read back by prefix (`GET /api/memories?namespace=auger&prefix=/auger/AUG176-code-factory/&limit=1000` -> 160 keys) and by `total` (2336 before, 2559 indexed), never asserted from a registration log alone. FAILIF: a count with no read-back command.","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-16T11:40:47.068852+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:44:48.315936+00:00","foreman_note":"AUG-178 — measured root cause, correcting this row's premise. Driver tick 2026-11-17T04:14-04:47Z.\n\nMEASURED: the hang was NOT caused by AUG-176's oversized ingest rows. Live namespace root is\n/home/kara/duckbrain/namespaces (NOT ~/.duckbrain-live, a stale copy — the earlier probe measured\nthe copy). auger's dir held a 0-byte `.search.rebuild.lock` (mtime 2026-11-01 03:28:45) and a\n`.search/` containing only `fts.duckdb.tmp` + `rows.tmp.jsonl` from 2026-10-30 — no sidecar, ever.\nEngine code src/search/index.ts:tryAcquireRebuildLock() steals only when\n`ageMs > STALE && pid !== null && !pidAlive(pid)`; an EMPTY lock parses to pid === null, so it is\nNEVER stolen → rebuildNamespaceIndex() waits for a lock that never vanishes → every ?q= and\n?contains= request hangs (client rc=124) while prefix reads stay fast (17-157 ms).\n\nFIX APPLIED (reversible housekeeping, auger only): the stale lock was moved to\n~/.hermes/goals/auger-stale-locks/a